WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.533
Model and RAG evals as regression tests.

2
00:00:03.833 --> 00:00:08.833
If you already have golden datasets and metrics, you're most of the way to a real test suite.

3
00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:14.233
An eval suite works just like a regression suite, with softer assertions.

4
00:00:14.533 --> 00:00:18.167
The golden set is versioned and frozen, like fixture files.

5
00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:22.667
We assert on scores with a tolerance band, not on strings with equality.

6
00:00:22.967 --> 00:00:24.785
And a score drop fails the build.

7
00:00:24.785 --> 00:00:27.100
It isn't a Slack thread three weeks later.

8
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:34.133
Faithfulness above zero point nine, averaged over the golden set, is the AI version of a snapshot test.

9
00:00:35.333 --> 00:00:36.400
Here is the gate.

10
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.833
Every prompt, model, or retriever change triggers it.

11
00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:42.667
The full golden set runs through the pipeline.

12
00:00:42.967 --> 00:00:45.867
Scores are compared with the baseline from the main branch.

13
00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:49.300
Only if they hold within tolerance can the change merge.

14
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.233
And here is the gate as a test.

15
00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:56.533
First, run the whole versioned golden set through the current pipeline.

16
00:00:56.833 --> 00:01:01.433
Faithfulness may not fall more than zero point zero two below the baseline.

17
00:01:01.733 --> 00:01:04.965
Recall and relevancy must stay above fixed floors.

18
00:01:04.965 --> 00:01:07.033
Fail the merge, don't just warn.

19
00:01:08.233 --> 00:01:09.900
Now the improvement that wasn't.

20
00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.933
A prompt tweak trims boilerplate, and it reads cleaner when you skim five examples.

21
00:01:15.233 --> 00:01:18.013
Run on the full golden set, faithfulness drops.

22
00:01:18.013 --> 00:01:22.567
The shorter prompt was quietly losing the cite your source chunk instruction.

23
00:01:22.867 --> 00:01:24.859
The gate blocks it before merge.

24
00:01:24.859 --> 00:01:29.467
After merge, that's a week of wondering why hallucination complaints rose.

25
00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:34.633
One trap: treating a score drop as a warning that someone may read later.

26
00:01:34.933 --> 00:01:37.267
Make it a failing check that blocks the merge.

27
00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:39.193
Let's recap.

28
00:01:39.193 --> 00:01:41.433
Your evals are your regression suite.

29
00:01:41.733 --> 00:01:44.967
Assert on scores with tolerance bands, not on strings.

30
00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:47.533
Keep the golden set versioned and frozen.

31
00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:50.703
And treat a score drop as a build failure.

32
00:01:50.703 --> 00:01:53.300
Next up: testing LLM outputs directly.
